      en: "The Ouadda Fortification is a French colonial military post built between 1935 and 1938 on a hill near the Sudanese border. It served as a strategic observation point and garrison. The fort features reinforced concrete walls, a watchtower, and barracks. It played a minor role in WWII. After independence, it was abandoned and fell into decay. The site offers panoramic views of the surrounding landscape. It is a significant example of colonial military architecture in remote Africa.",
